    "slug": "modes-half-steps",
    "title": "Where the Half Steps Fall",
    "summary": "Every mode has the same five whole steps and two half steps — a mode is decided by where the two tight spots sit next to home.",
    "tags": ["modes", "theory", "ear"],
    "readingTimeMin": 3,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-15"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seven notes, five whole steps, two half steps — every one of the seven modes has exactly that ingredient list, and it never changes. What changes from mode to mode is where the two tight spots sit relative to the note you're calling home. That's the whole lesson: not how many half steps a mode has, but their address."
        }
      ]
